# KNOWN GAP — ICE (compiler panic, exit 101) at IR lowering: re-throwing the
# `catch` error-binding from inside a `match` ARM panics the Tier 2a
# consume-site validator.
#
#     thread 'gg-main' panicked at src/ir/lowering/mod.rs:2114:
#     Tier 2a consume-site violation: 1 violation(s) in module '<unknown>'.
#     First: fn @handle bb2 i4 — AssignIntoOwnedSlot(dst: CE) —
#     owned-but-live source consumed without preceding clone.
#
# The `match` arm is load-bearing. Measured at filing (all via `gg build`, NOT
# `gg check` — the panic is in IR lowering, which `check` never reaches):
#   - `throw e` bare in the catch block .................... OK
#   - `throw e` inside an `if` in the catch block .......... OK
#   - `match e` in the catch block with NO `throw` ......... OK
#   - `throw e` inside a `match` ARM ...................... ICE  <- this file
# Enum arity is NOT the discriminator (reproduces with one variant and two).
#
# Why it matters beyond the crash: this is the natural idiom for PARTIAL error
# handling — recover from some variants, re-throw the rest. The Result-capture
# spelling (`Result[T,E] r = f()` + `match r: case Error(CE.NotFound(_)): ...`)
# works correctly and is the current workaround, so this is an ergonomics gap
# wearing an ICE, not a missing capability.
#
# Distinct from the filed Tier 2a siblings: TODO's `s.debug()` panic is a
# different site (`mod.rs:2084`) and a builtin-method trigger; the Dict/Set
# `put`/`insert` consume-classification item is a check-time REJECT, not an ICE;
# the self-host `lower_catch_expr` err-binding item is an SH-lane verify-by-
# running task, whereas this is a Rust-gg lowering panic.
#
# INTENDED behavior: `load("x")` throws `CE.NotFound("x")`; the catch binds it,
# the match takes the `NotFound` arm, and the recovery value is 8080 — so the
# program prints 8080 and exits 0. It must NOT panic the compiler.

enum CE:
    NotFound(String)
    BadPort(int)

int load(String p) throws CE:
    throw CE.NotFound(p)

int handle(String p) throws CE:
    int c = load(p)! catch (e):
        match e:
            case CE.NotFound(_):
                8080
            else:
                throw e
    return c

void main():
    print(handle("x")! catch (_): -1)
